        "title": "refactor(ui): remove dead exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe shrink-only dead-export ratchet carried 363 `ui/` entries on current `main`, allowing unused Control UI exports to remain indefinitely. The task began at 365; `main` independently removed two realtime type exports in #106221 while this branch was being rebased.\n\nCloses #105791\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Internalize unused Control UI symbols and delete helpers or tests that existed only for those exports.\n- Keep meaningful behavior coverage through production-owned modules and public component boundaries.\n- Split custom-element registration side effects where production consumers need implementation exports.\n- Preserve current-main Control UI refactors while repeatedly absorbing baseline drift.\n- Regenerate the baseline with no remaining entry whose path starts with `ui/`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. The Control UI exposes a smaller internal module surface while retaining reconnect, registration, chat, workspace, plugin, and navigation behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Final current-main baseline reconciliation: 3,346 entries to 2,983; exactly 363 remaining `ui/` entries removed; zero non-UI removals and zero additions.\n- Combined task result: all 365 originally observed UI entries are gone; two landed independently in #106221 and this PR removes the remaining 363.\n- Static audit of the original 365 findings: 355 declarations internalized/deleted (two now on `main`); 10 implementation exports now have production callers through registration or lazy-loader boundaries.\n- `pnpm test:ui`: 238 files, 3,538 tests passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:ui`, `pnpm tsgo:test:ui`, and `pnpm build` passed.\n- Focused Control UI Chromium E2E: 7 files, 77 tests passed, covering chat flow, session management, sidebar customization, approval routing, login gating, initial connection, and mount recovery.\n- Remote proof: [Crabbox run run_2c616159ce2d](https://crabbox.openclaw.ai/portal/runs/run_2c616159ce2d).\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs --update` regenerated 2,983 entries; the subsequent check matched exactly. `git diff --check` and baseline module syntax passed.\n- Final published tree SHA matches the frozen local tree exactly: `7b7747adaf2b0fe091382c70759593f2ac38c72d`.\n- Exact PR head: `6ecaa5bbc4b2225fd8e068730bb6c9954d04be7a`; hosted CI and exact-head Mantis browser proof are pending.\n- The whole 796 KB branch exceeds the autoreview helper's 180 KB fail-closed bundle limit; coherent production, registration, page/baseline, and test/lib surface reviews were clean before the final rebase. The final CI repair is separately reviewable.\n- Actual built-Gateway lifecycle smoke could not be rerun after the final rebase because the task sandbox blocked outbound Crabbox/AWS access. Chromium E2E and Mantis use the repository's mocked Gateway harness; hosted CI is the final exact-head gate.\n",
